{title: A Mighty Fortress Is Our God}
{artist: Martin Luther / Frederick Hedge (trans.)}
{genre: Hymn}
{flow: Opening}
{style: Traditional}
{key: C}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 4/4}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 585장}
{title_ko: 내 주는 강한 성이요}
{score: a-mighty-fortress.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]A mighty fortress [G]is our [C]God
A [F]bulwark never [C]failing
Our [Am]helper He, a[G]mid the [C]flood
Of [F]mortal ills pre[G]vailing
For [C]still our ancient [G]foe
Doth [Am]seek to work us [G]woe
His [C]craft and power are [F]great
And [C]armed with cruel [G]hate
On [C]earth is not his [G]equal [C]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Did we in our own [G]strength con[C]fide
Our [F]striving would be [C]losing
Were [Am]not the right Man [G]on our [C]side
The [F]Man of God's own [G]choosing
Dost [C]ask who that may [G]be
Christ [Am]Jesus, it is [G]He
Lord [C]Sabaoth, His [F]name
From [C]age to age the [G]same
And [C]He must win the [G]bat[C]tle
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]And though this world, with [G]devils [C]filled
Should [F]threaten to un[C]do us
We [Am]will not fear, for [G]God hath [C]willed
His [F]truth to triumph [G]through us
The [C]Prince of Darkness [G]grim
We [Am]tremble not for [G]him
His [C]rage we can en[F]dure
For [C]lo! his doom is [G]sure
One [C]little word shall [G]fell [C]him
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]That word above all [G]earthly [C]powers
No [F]thanks to them, a[C]bideth
The [Am]Spirit and the [G]gifts are [C]ours
Through [F]Him who with us [G]sideth
Let [C]goods and kindred [G]go
This [Am]mortal life al[G]so
The [C]body they may [F]kill
God's [C]truth abideth [G]still
His [C]kingdom is for[G]ev[C]er
{end_of_verse}
